// Mobs of the base game. Models are made of boxes measured in pixels (1/16 of a block).
// Model space: origin at the feet, +Y up, +Z is the direction the mob faces.
// `origin` is the box's minimum corner. `uv` is where the box's unwrap starts in the 64×64 skin:
//   top at (u+d, v) w×d, bottom at (u+d+w, v) w×d,
//   right side (-X) at (u, v+d) d×h, front (+Z) at (u+d, v+d) w×h,
//   left side (+X) at (u+d+w, v+d) d×h, back (-Z) at (u+2d+w, v+d) w×h.
// `pivot` is the point a part rotates around when it is animated.
//
// Skins are 64×128. The top half holds the parts above; the bottom half (v + 64) holds the
// `layers`: an overlay for a part, drawn as real 3D relief (every opaque pixel becomes a small
// block standing `inflate` pixels off the body), so wool, fur, hair and torn clothes have volume
// instead of being painted flat. Transparent pixels in a layer are simply empty.
(mobs: [
    (
        name: "pig", display_name: "Porco", kind: Passive, health: 10, speed: 2.4,
        drops: [(item: "porkchop", min: 1, max: 3)], xp: 2,
        width: 0.9, height: 0.9, spawn: Grass,
        parts: [
            (size: (10, 8, 16), origin: (-5, 6, -8), uv: (0, 0)),
            (size: (8, 8, 8), origin: (-4, 8, 7), uv: (0, 24), anim: Head, pivot: (0, 12, 8)),
            (size: (4, 3, 1), origin: (-2, 9, 15), uv: (32, 24), anim: Head, pivot: (0, 12, 8)),
            (size: (4, 6, 4), origin: (-5, 0, -7), uv: (0, 40), anim: Leg(0), pivot: (-3, 6, -5)),
            (size: (4, 6, 4), origin: (1, 0, -7), uv: (0, 40), anim: Leg(1), pivot: (3, 6, -5)),
            (size: (4, 6, 4), origin: (-5, 0, 3), uv: (0, 40), anim: Leg(1), pivot: (-3, 6, 5)),
            (size: (4, 6, 4), origin: (1, 0, 3), uv: (0, 40), anim: Leg(0), pivot: (3, 6, 5)),
        ],
        layers: [(part: 0, inflate: 0.5), (part: 1, inflate: 0.5)],
    ),
